1
00:00:02,580 --> 00:00:05,420
We've only got a week left 
until the prelims start.

2
00:00:05,420 --> 00:00:07,250
But nothing we can do right now.

3
00:00:08,040 --> 00:00:10,290
Why don't we just practice 
in the hallway again?

4
00:00:10,290 --> 00:00:12,100
We got in trouble for that last time.

5
00:00:12,100 --> 00:00:14,150
They bitched at us for all the 
squeaky noise our shoes were making.

6
00:00:14,330 --> 00:00:16,380
Doesn't this school have a 
training room or something?

7
00:00:16,500 --> 00:00:19,460
Kuzu High isn't some prestigious school
with fancy shit like that.

8
00:00:20,750 --> 00:00:23,540
We wait until either the volleyball team
finishes using the court.

9
00:00:23,540 --> 00:00:25,630
Or the rain lets up.

10
00:00:25,920 --> 00:00:28,540
What a waste of a precious Saturday.

11
00:00:29,460 --> 00:00:30,250
Okay!

12
00:00:30,250 --> 00:00:31,250
Memorize these!

13
00:00:31,670 --> 00:00:34,170
Uh, let's see, Nanao has a 4.

14
00:00:34,170 --> 00:00:37,830
Yasuhara has an 11, no wait, a 14 I think?

15
00:00:37,830 --> 00:00:39,750
And, uh, Chucky has a...

16
00:00:41,040 --> 00:00:42,290
A woman.

17
00:00:42,290 --> 00:00:43,210
Wow.

18
00:00:43,210 --> 00:00:45,830
How on Earth could you know that
when your back is facing us?!

19
00:00:45,830 --> 00:00:47,580
It's gotta be a trick of 
some kind, I just know it!

20
00:00:48,040 --> 00:00:50,880
You always fail 'cuz you try
to memorize them one-by-one.

21
00:00:50,880 --> 00:00:54,710
You'll never be a good point guard
unless you learn to look at the bigger picture.

22
00:00:55,920 --> 00:00:59,420
Just imagine you had to pick
your favorite girl out of 100 of them,

23
00:00:59,420 --> 00:01:02,040
you gotta be able to decide at just a glance
or they won't be impressed.

24
00:01:02,210 --> 00:01:06,080
You don't have to worry about that happening,
because it's a complete fantasy!

25
00:01:06,080 --> 00:01:07,800
Besides, I'm not a horse.

26
00:01:07,800 --> 00:01:09,880
I don't have monocular vision
that lets me see both front and back!

27
00:01:09,880 --> 00:01:12,630
Dude, did you seriously 
just compare me to a horse?

28
00:01:12,630 --> 00:01:14,330
Brace yourself for my 
patented Rock Chop later!

29
00:01:14,330 --> 00:01:16,540
"Patented"? That's just 
a plain old punch, man.

30
00:01:17,000 --> 00:01:19,710
But damn, the rain just won't let up today.

31
00:01:19,710 --> 00:01:23,330
That's fine by me.
We need a break from practice sometimes.

32
00:01:23,540 --> 00:01:26,790
I guess this is the best a 
regular high school can offer.

33
00:01:27,790 --> 00:01:31,210
Does this team really stand 
any chance... at winning?

34
00:01:32,670 --> 00:01:33,880
Um, hey.

35
00:01:34,330 --> 00:01:35,250
Huh?

36
00:01:35,250 --> 00:01:37,420
We're going to wrap up 
our practice for today.

37
00:01:37,580 --> 00:01:39,210
Here are the keys for the gym.

38
00:01:40,000 --> 00:01:42,710
Are you sure? You've only been using it
for about an hour...

39
00:01:43,000 --> 00:01:44,670
The rain ruined everything.

40
00:01:44,670 --> 00:01:46,580
Most of our members didn't even show up.

41
00:01:46,580 --> 00:01:48,420
And we've got midterm 
tests next week, anyway.

42
00:01:48,630 --> 00:01:51,420
The badminton team also 
started packing up early.

43
00:01:52,830 --> 00:01:55,080
I guess we do get lucky sometimes!

44
00:01:55,080 --> 00:01:58,130
This means we can use the 
whole court all we want!

45
00:01:58,290 --> 00:02:00,530
Uh, that's great, but shouldn't some of you

46
00:02:00,530 --> 00:02:02,500
be studying for the upcoming tests, too?

47
00:02:02,500 --> 00:02:04,330
Ain't nothing to worry about!

48
00:02:04,750 --> 00:02:07,580
Oh really? I guess you guys 
must be pretty smart, then.

49
00:02:07,670 --> 00:02:09,420
Haha! That's a laugh!

50
00:02:09,420 --> 00:02:11,710
I'm gonna bomb all the tests 
just like I always do!

51
00:02:12,000 --> 00:02:13,920
That's not something to be proud of!

52
00:02:20,500 --> 00:02:22,130
It's Shigeyoshi...

53
00:02:23,330 --> 00:02:31,210
Kagami ni senaka mukete ayumu 
hodo ni toozakaru yume yo

54
00:02:31,210 --> 00:02:35,670
Massugu kimi to mukiaitai

55
00:02:36,000 --> 00:02:42,290
Dekinai jibun e to "never mind"

56
00:02:44,000 --> 00:02:50,080
Ahiru no Sora

57
00:02:51,750 --> 00:02:56,130
Nagare sagyou de waketeyuku yume

58
00:02:57,000 --> 00:02:59,420
Muki? Fumuki? Iwaba rongai?

59
00:02:59,500 --> 00:03:03,830
Koe mo naku kietetta koe

60
00:03:04,420 --> 00:03:06,830
Tameiki sura denai

61
00:03:07,210 --> 00:03:13,040
Hito no sei ni shitatte owarenai

62
00:03:13,210 --> 00:03:17,000
Me no mae ni kiritatta ima

63
00:03:17,000 --> 00:03:21,040
"Koetai" to kokoro ga sakenderu

64
00:03:21,040 --> 00:03:28,580
Dekinai wake o sagasu nara daredemo dekiru sa

65
00:03:28,790 --> 00:03:36,130
Agaki hashitta sono saki 
mada shiranai jibun to deau

66
00:03:36,420 --> 00:03:42,500
Kabe ni kizamikonda rakugaki to "never mind"

67
00:03:42,670 --> 00:03:46,580
Ima asu e to hazume

68
00:03:53,830 --> 00:03:57,790
Light

69
00:03:54,000 --> 00:03:57,380
Nobody was here, so I thought 
you canceled practice.

70
00:03:57,500 --> 00:03:58,500
Ah, no.

71
00:03:58,500 --> 00:04:00,500
We take turns using the 
gym with the other teams.

72
00:04:00,920 --> 00:04:02,290
Lemme help you out!

73
00:04:02,290 --> 00:04:03,750
Uh, thank you.

74
00:04:03,960 --> 00:04:06,170
We have free reign of the gym for once.

75
00:04:06,170 --> 00:04:07,790
Let's lower the glass boards in the middle.

76
00:04:07,790 --> 00:04:10,160
Sure, we'll rock-paper-scissors
for who does the hard work.

77
00:04:10,160 --> 00:04:11,120
Here we go!

78
00:04:11,250 --> 00:04:14,380
Rock, paper, scissors...!

79
00:04:13,170 --> 00:04:14,380
Shoot!

80
00:04:14,380 --> 00:04:17,130
Please allow me to join the basketball team.

81
00:04:21,580 --> 00:04:24,460
I would like to apologize 
for lying to all of you.

82
00:04:24,670 --> 00:04:26,380
Shigeyoshi...

83
00:04:26,380 --> 00:04:28,670
I'm sorry. Please forgive me.

84
00:04:29,580 --> 00:04:32,000
But, the truth is...

85
00:04:32,000 --> 00:04:34,460
...I want to get serious about 
playing basketball again.

86
00:04:36,000 --> 00:04:37,080
Please let me join.

87
00:04:37,580 --> 00:04:38,710
Hold up.

88
00:04:39,210 --> 00:04:41,080
We've already seen your true colors.

89
00:04:41,080 --> 00:04:42,880
You can't expect to just 
smooth talk your way in now.

90
00:04:43,330 --> 00:04:44,080
Kite.

91
00:04:44,080 --> 00:04:48,130
Despite how our team looks,
we're working really damn hard to reach the top.

92
00:04:48,630 --> 00:04:52,000
Your half-assed passion for the game
is just gonna drag us down.

93
00:04:52,000 --> 00:04:53,330
Go back to playing chemist, fool.

94
00:04:53,630 --> 00:04:56,210
Hey! Be nice, Natsume!
You don't have to act so rude all the-

95
00:04:56,210 --> 00:04:58,630
We're wasting precious time. 
Let's get to practicing.

96
00:04:58,880 --> 00:05:00,210
R-right...

97
00:05:06,130 --> 00:05:10,040
The reason I came here...
is because I have true passion for the game.

98
00:05:13,500 --> 00:05:16,460
I'm serious. I want to play basketball.

99
00:05:18,460 --> 00:05:20,330
But what about the chemistry club?

100
00:05:20,830 --> 00:05:24,630
I just finished turning in
my formal resignation to the club advisor.

101
00:05:25,250 --> 00:05:27,790
There's nowhere else for me to go now.

102
00:05:28,040 --> 00:05:29,500
Please allow me to stay with you.

103
00:05:29,500 --> 00:05:30,830
You're not an orphan, jeez.

104
00:05:31,290 --> 00:05:34,540
Since he's this insistent about it,
I don't see any reason to say no.

105
00:05:34,540 --> 00:05:36,210
It's just fine by me, personally.

106
00:05:37,830 --> 00:05:39,040
I don't agree.

107
00:05:40,000 --> 00:05:41,460
Kurumatani...

108
00:05:42,290 --> 00:05:45,380
I can't bring myself to believe him
when he claims to be "serious."

109
00:05:47,210 --> 00:05:48,710
Color me surprised.

110
00:05:48,710 --> 00:05:50,790
Tinytown is totally picking a fight, guys.

111
00:05:51,040 --> 00:05:52,960
Then how can I convince you?

112
00:05:56,710 --> 00:05:57,830
Come out on the court.

113
00:05:59,000 --> 00:06:00,290
Is this for real?

114
00:06:02,920 --> 00:06:05,210
Okay. I get it.

115
00:06:09,710 --> 00:06:10,630
He's fast!

116
00:06:13,380 --> 00:06:15,170
Whoa! A double frappÃ©!

117
00:06:15,420 --> 00:06:16,920
It's a double clutch, dude.

118
00:06:18,670 --> 00:06:20,040
That's one basket for me.

119
00:06:22,420 --> 00:06:25,070
I see... blocks are inevitable for him,

120
00:06:25,070 --> 00:06:27,150
so his playstyle is all 
about dealing with them.

121
00:06:29,130 --> 00:06:31,500
This is like watching an adult play a kid.

122
00:06:31,500 --> 00:06:33,910
It doesn't matter how good 
Kurumatani is on the court,

123
00:06:33,910 --> 00:06:35,950
he won't be able to stop Shigeyoshi's shots.

124
00:06:36,380 --> 00:06:38,040
There's just too much of a gap in height.

125
00:06:38,460 --> 00:06:40,750
It doesn't matter.
Their skills will be what decide this match.

126
00:06:44,750 --> 00:06:46,670
Whoa, that was a smooth move!

127
00:06:49,460 --> 00:06:51,500
And now, we're even.

128
00:06:54,000 --> 00:06:57,170
Is it just me, or is Kurumatani acting
a little strange today?

129
00:06:57,460 --> 00:07:00,420
He was the one most excited about the idea
of Shigeyoshi joining us.

130
00:07:01,170 --> 00:07:04,630
Did he just get really upset 
at being lied to, or what?

131
00:07:09,380 --> 00:07:12,420
You should be... guarding me more closely.

132
00:07:12,580 --> 00:07:13,170
Huh?

133
00:07:19,500 --> 00:07:21,380
I'm not missing a single shot today.

134
00:07:23,210 --> 00:07:25,750
He scored from long-range 
on me in a one-on-one...

135
00:07:27,330 --> 00:07:27,960
Dammit!

136
00:07:31,750 --> 00:07:32,330
There it is!

137
00:07:42,460 --> 00:07:43,830
What's the matter?

138
00:07:43,830 --> 00:07:45,630
We've barely been at it for 10 minutes.

139
00:07:46,920 --> 00:07:48,670
Is this really how you play 
when you're "serious"?

140
00:07:50,380 --> 00:07:52,080
A'ight! That's enough!

141
00:07:52,080 --> 00:07:55,080
We can't waste any more time.
Get ready to start practice!

142
00:07:56,540 --> 00:07:58,750
Hey! I think this guy 
is at his limit already.

143
00:07:58,920 --> 00:08:00,500
What? No...

144
00:08:00,500 --> 00:08:02,080
Hit the bench and rest up.

145
00:08:02,080 --> 00:08:03,330
But I...

146
00:08:03,330 --> 00:08:04,330
You're in the way!

147
00:08:04,750 --> 00:08:06,290
Sekiya! Sub out with him!

148
00:08:06,460 --> 00:08:08,210
Hold it right there!

149
00:08:08,580 --> 00:08:09,460
Ow!

150
00:08:09,460 --> 00:08:11,290
Whoa! The girls are invading our turf!

151
00:08:11,290 --> 00:08:13,330
Why are you guys bullying 
the new guy like that?

152
00:08:13,750 --> 00:08:16,790
Don't the freshman have
their own training schedule to follow?

153
00:08:16,790 --> 00:08:17,790
Jerks.

154
00:08:17,790 --> 00:08:20,170
Yeah, well, this guy doesn't 
even look like a freshman.

155
00:08:21,130 --> 00:08:23,460
Speak up for yourself when you need a break.

156
00:08:24,420 --> 00:08:27,540
Don't let anybody else determine 
what your limits are.

157
00:08:28,750 --> 00:08:29,790
Senpai...

158
00:08:34,080 --> 00:08:35,210
I'm not done yet.

159
00:08:37,040 --> 00:08:38,960
I can still keep playing.

160
00:08:52,210 --> 00:08:55,000
Oh my gosh... that was 
high enough to be a dunk!

161
00:08:56,130 --> 00:08:58,130
And now, we're even once again.

162
00:08:58,420 --> 00:09:00,670
That was definitely a foul. Just now.

163
00:09:01,290 --> 00:09:04,420
No way, that's typical contact 
for under the basket.

164
00:09:08,250 --> 00:09:10,710
They've been at it for 30 minutes already.

165
00:09:10,710 --> 00:09:13,420
That Mokichi guy is pretty 
decent for hanging on so long.

166
00:09:13,420 --> 00:09:14,080
Yeah.

167
00:09:14,460 --> 00:09:16,670
He's just trying to skip 
out on actual practice.

168
00:09:17,250 --> 00:09:19,420
I knew a guy like that back in middle school.

169
00:09:20,630 --> 00:09:23,290
It definitely doesn't seem 
that way to me, though.

170
00:09:23,290 --> 00:09:23,750
Huh?

171
00:09:24,040 --> 00:09:27,000
That guy has gone... well beyond his limit.

172
00:09:29,790 --> 00:09:30,540
A crossover!

173
00:09:46,080 --> 00:09:48,130
Not yet. Let's keep going.

174
00:09:55,210 --> 00:09:58,250
I'm sick and tired... of shouldering 
people's expectations.

175
00:09:59,130 --> 00:10:02,670
And I'm already used...
to people being disappointed in me.

176
00:10:04,210 --> 00:10:07,670
But... the truth is...

177
00:10:08,250 --> 00:10:09,880
none of that ever really 
mattered to me at all.

178
00:10:13,750 --> 00:10:17,710
All of the seniors... on the day
of our very last tournament together...

179
00:10:20,710 --> 00:10:21,750
I've gotta block!

180
00:10:32,540 --> 00:10:34,500
Saijo
Kozu

181
00:11:13,960 --> 00:11:15,290
Tsukishima...

182
00:11:17,210 --> 00:11:19,460
What I feared more than anything...

183
00:11:20,580 --> 00:11:22,580
was losing the light you brought.

184
00:11:33,580 --> 00:11:36,210
Holy shit, check that dunk! Badass!

185
00:11:37,380 --> 00:11:40,630
He plays pretty rough 
despite looking so timid.

186
00:11:40,630 --> 00:11:42,000
He's showing off too damn much.

187
00:11:44,750 --> 00:11:47,500
Looks like... I win.

188
00:11:47,750 --> 00:11:49,080
He just smiled!

189
00:11:49,080 --> 00:11:50,830
I didn't think that was possible for him!

190
00:11:50,830 --> 00:11:52,750
What the hell gave you that impression?

191
00:11:52,880 --> 00:11:54,460
Shigeyoshi...

192
00:11:56,000 --> 00:11:57,040
Smug jerk...

193
00:11:59,170 --> 00:12:00,790
I looked up the word "regret"...

194
00:12:04,460 --> 00:12:06,000
...in the dictionary.

195
00:12:08,290 --> 00:12:11,420
I realized... I was an idiot.

196
00:12:12,580 --> 00:12:13,830
See ya.

197
00:12:13,830 --> 00:12:14,750
Bye.

198
00:12:25,170 --> 00:12:26,710
Wait, isn't this your friend, Kyoko?

199
00:12:26,710 --> 00:12:28,750
How terrible, don't you have an umbrella?

200
00:12:30,420 --> 00:12:33,290
I forgot mine... back at school.

201
00:12:33,290 --> 00:12:35,080
Even though it's raining so hard?

202
00:12:35,080 --> 00:12:36,670
Quick, find a towel!

203
00:12:39,880 --> 00:12:44,040
The truth is... that I did like 
you back then, Tsukishima.

204
00:12:45,710 --> 00:12:47,920
Yeah. I know.

205
00:12:48,670 --> 00:12:51,000
And... I still do now.

206
00:12:53,330 --> 00:12:54,790
I know that, too.

207
00:13:02,080 --> 00:13:02,670
Goodbye.

208
00:13:02,960 --> 00:13:04,500
Wait, Kyoko!

209
00:13:04,500 --> 00:13:05,830
What's with you?

210
00:13:05,830 --> 00:13:08,960
I don't know what's going on,
but you're being way too hard on him.

211
00:13:09,830 --> 00:13:12,210
You should at least listen 
to what he has to say.

212
00:13:13,420 --> 00:13:18,130
Senpai... I've decided
to start playing basketball once again.

213
00:13:18,710 --> 00:13:20,490
If things go well,

214
00:13:20,490 --> 00:13:23,820
my team will go up against
the one from your school in the second round.

215
00:13:25,040 --> 00:13:28,130
A huge mistake... that I'll 
never be able to undo.

216
00:13:29,250 --> 00:13:32,670
That is the burden... with 
which I must live with.

217
00:13:39,920 --> 00:13:41,790
That was so mean of you, Kurumatani.

218
00:13:42,210 --> 00:13:45,380
Shigeyoshi actually came to us
without needing any convincing.

219
00:13:45,880 --> 00:13:48,080
Don't you want to play on 
the same team with him?

220
00:13:49,500 --> 00:13:52,240
I think... there really are 
people in the world too sick

221
00:13:52,240 --> 00:13:54,780
to play basketball even though they want to.

222
00:13:55,390 --> 00:13:59,580
That's why... it was impossible for me
to just forgive Mokichi for lying about that.

223
00:14:00,670 --> 00:14:02,290
Kurumatani...

224
00:14:02,290 --> 00:14:03,170
But...

225
00:14:04,960 --> 00:14:06,380
...I'm glad it wasn't true.

226
00:14:07,540 --> 00:14:12,080
In the end, I still really do want to play basketball...
together with Mokichi.

227
00:14:15,210 --> 00:14:17,040
We have a new member I 
need to introduce to you.

228
00:14:19,210 --> 00:14:21,250
Or at least, I wanted to, but...

229
00:14:21,460 --> 00:14:23,130
...he's apparently out 
sick with a cold today.

230
00:14:24,420 --> 00:14:25,210
You gotta be kidding!

231
00:14:25,710 --> 00:14:28,000
So now, I'll just skip 
to today's announcements.

232
00:14:28,290 --> 00:14:31,750
As you all know, the midterm 
tests will begin tomorrow.

233
00:14:32,170 --> 00:14:35,670
Generally speaking, all teams are on break
during the testing period...

234
00:14:35,830 --> 00:14:36,710
What?!

235
00:14:36,710 --> 00:14:38,580
Wha-?! Hold on a damn second!

236
00:14:38,790 --> 00:14:41,250
We only have 6 days left 
until the prelims start!

237
00:14:41,420 --> 00:14:43,790
And I still haven't been able 
to get my shots to go in!

238
00:14:44,040 --> 00:14:46,830
If we stop practicing this 
week then we're doomed!

239
00:14:46,830 --> 00:14:47,920
Ban the tests instead!

240
00:14:48,580 --> 00:14:51,420
I'm fully aware. Relax, 
I'm not a complete tyrant.

241
00:14:52,000 --> 00:14:54,380
For the following four days that 
the tests are being held...

242
00:14:54,380 --> 00:14:57,880
...you boys are free to make use
of the empty gym in whatever way you see fit.

243
00:14:58,670 --> 00:15:00,420
Oh sweet, that's an awesome deal.

244
00:15:00,420 --> 00:15:01,630
This is perfect.

245
00:15:01,630 --> 00:15:04,040
Especially since school gets out at noon
during test week!

246
00:15:04,040 --> 00:15:06,040
It'll be like a mini training camp!

247
00:15:06,040 --> 00:15:08,670
That means we'll be able to 
pack our schedule totally full.

248
00:15:08,670 --> 00:15:09,540
For sure!

249
00:15:10,130 --> 00:15:13,130
Midterms! For the win! Yes!

250
00:15:13,130 --> 00:15:14,710
Uh, just one more thing.

251
00:15:15,210 --> 00:15:18,620
If any of you end up with a failing grade
on the midterm tests,

252
00:15:18,620 --> 00:15:20,190
I'll pull you from the prelims.

253
00:15:22,330 --> 00:15:23,540
Seriously...?

254
00:15:23,540 --> 00:15:24,670
Dead serious.

255
00:15:25,000 --> 00:15:27,670
WHAAAAT?!

256
00:15:27,920 --> 00:15:30,210
Okay, that's a big problem.

257
00:15:30,210 --> 00:15:33,000
For now, just raise your hand 
if you expect to fail a test.

258
00:15:33,170 --> 00:15:34,130
Okay!

259
00:15:34,130 --> 00:15:36,580
That's basically the entire team!

260
00:15:36,830 --> 00:15:39,580
What about that Mokichi guy who just joined?

261
00:15:39,580 --> 00:15:42,210
Maybe we can drop him 
before he ruins it for us.

262
00:15:42,210 --> 00:15:44,460
Worry about yourselves first!

263
00:15:44,460 --> 00:15:46,380
Shigeyoshi went to THE Saijo Middle School,

264
00:15:46,380 --> 00:15:48,920
so he must be plenty smart and talented!

265
00:15:48,920 --> 00:15:49,670
For real?!

266
00:15:49,670 --> 00:15:51,580
Jeez, what a damn glory hound!

267
00:15:52,210 --> 00:15:54,990
Anyways, I think our best 
bet is to focus on just

268
00:15:54,990 --> 00:15:57,490
the key subjects and study 
in groups split by grade.

269
00:15:58,080 --> 00:15:59,500
What tests are tomorrow?

270
00:15:59,500 --> 00:16:02,290
Do you all know what to expect?
Have you been taking notes in class?

271
00:16:02,790 --> 00:16:03,630
Nope.

272
00:16:03,630 --> 00:16:04,420
Beats me.

273
00:16:04,420 --> 00:16:05,460
Who uses notebooks?

274
00:16:05,830 --> 00:16:08,250
You can memorize info by 
eating textbooks, you know.

275
00:16:08,250 --> 00:16:11,170
P-please give me a few pages!
I'll top them with some mayo!

276
00:16:11,710 --> 00:16:16,420
So hey, "Kings of the Animal Jungle" is on tonight.
Can I go home early?

277
00:16:16,420 --> 00:16:19,250
Okay, I've had it up to HERE with you guys!

278
00:16:19,500 --> 00:16:23,420
Starting right now, NOBODY can leave the gym
without my express permission!

279
00:16:23,420 --> 00:16:24,630
HUH?!

